erage gap identification\n    # Trend analysis\n```\n\n## Success Validation\n\n### Final Acceptance Criteria\n1. **Error Handling Coverage**: 100% for BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n2. **Performance Improvement**: Success rate >90%, iterations <8 per task\n3. **Test Coverage**: >95% code coverage\n4. **Zero Regression**: No degradation in existing functionality\n5. **Documentation**: Complete test documentation and runbooks\n\nThis comprehensive test strategy ensures the error handling implementation meets all performance and reliability requirements while maintaining system stability and user experience.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NPYAHjL1gTptiXjeDtoQyS', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to output/error_handling_test_strategy.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': "You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 53.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you're using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully located the Development Manager agent definition file and verified the max iterations settin